                        author "brendan@bbqsrc.net"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Select polling 3.11.0 as the narrow Unix readiness reactor for Ronin's explicit process supervisor; do not add Tokio. On the interleaved 1,024-child, -j256 production A/B, evented Ronin reduced median wall time from 382.507 ms to 356.733 ms, coordinator peak threads from 270 to 1, and peak RSS from 8,300 KiB to 4,652 KiB. The isolated evented probe added 1.0% binary size versus 38.7% for current-thread Tokio, while the idle-heavy probe needed 246 readiness wakes versus 1,589 busy scan iterations. This instantiates rather than supersedes [dec:ronin:completion-driven-execution]: the scheduler remains one explicit completion-driven supervisor without a general async runtime. Cache load-average reads for 100 ms and flush output sinks only after complete status/failure/output batches."
                    }
                )
            }

