                        kind @decision
                        text "Keep rapidhash; fix how it is written. Replacing the algorithm was considered and rejected: Ninja itself hashes build-log commands with rapidhash (src/build_log.cc HashCommand, src/hash_map.h), so the value written to .ninja_log is a cross-tool contract — any other hash makes every edge read as command-line-changed the first time a tree switches between ninja and ronin, causing a full spurious rebuild. The NodeIndex hash is internal and free to change, but rapidhash is already at the fast end for the 10-40 byte paths it sees, so xxhash buys nothing there and costs a dependency. Callgrind on the current build puts rapidhashv1 at 3.9% of the wide no-op build and 3.4% of deep-graph evaluation, roughly 116 instructions to hash a ten-byte path where 20-30 is achievable. Suspected causes: mum() converts both halves of the u128 product with fallible try_from().expect() on the hottest arithmetic in the function, and every 4- and 8-byte read goes through the RapidBytes trait's contiguous() returning Option plus a try_into().expect(), where the segmented implementation used for command hashing may be defeating specialisation for the contiguous case."
                    }

