            {
                id make-vpath-name-reaches-a-recipe-read-early
                title "Spell a searched-for prerequisite in a recipe the compiler had to read"
                kind @fix
                deps (make-vpath-name-survives-only-a-current-target)
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-08-22T04:46:01.785002374Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Found while delivering make-vpath-name-survives-only-a-current-target, measured against the pristine 4.4.1 oracle, and left out of it because it is a second mechanism rather than a condition that node gets wrong.\n\nA target the directory search found elsewhere carries both names until the build settles which one it has, and the settled spelling reaches a recipe because Ronin expands Make recipes at LAUNCH. Four shapes take that away — a recursive `$(MAKE)`, a depfile, a grouped double-colon action, and a recipe naming `$?` — because the compiler has to read those recipes for itself while the graph is being built. The prerequisite names in such a recipe are settled into its text there and then, long before anything knows whether the target had to be remade.\n\nReproducer, with an empty `build/` holding a `build/out.o` NEWER than `out.c`:\n\n  VPATH = build\n  all: out.o ; @printf 'whole [%s] new [%s] first [%s]\\n' '$^' '$?' '$<' > seen\n  out.o: out.c ; @printf 'made\\n' > $@\n\nGNU Make leaves `whole [build/out.o] new [build/out.o] first [build/out.o]`. Ronin leaves `whole [out.o] new [build/out.o] first [out.o]`.\n\n`$?` is right and the other three are wrong, and the split is the mechanism itself. `$?` is not in the text at all: the recipe holds `${KATI_NEW_INPUTS}` and the scheduler substitutes the names when the edge launches, so the settled spelling reaches it through `DeferredFreshness` — which is where the delivering node taught it to. `$^`, `$<`, `$+` and their `D`/`F` forms are bytes the early read wrote, and there is nothing left to substitute into.\n\nWHAT A FIX LOOKS LIKE, having checked the pieces. The substitution machinery already exists and is per-edge: `resolve_deferred_new_inputs` replaces `${NAME}` in a launch command, and an early-read recipe naming `$?` HAS a `DeferredFreshness` to hang more names off. So the shape is a reference per searched-for prerequisite — kati emitting one where `AutoCommandVar::eval_impl` would have written the name, the pair reaching `SinkEdge` beside `deferred_new_input_names`, and the executor substituting the spelling this build settled on. What is missing on kati's side is that a dependent's `DepNode` does not carry its inputs' found paths: `DepNode::searched_at` is the node's own, so the per-input list has to be recorded when `resolve_vpaths` runs.\n\nThe other three early-read shapes were NOT probed and may not be reachable at all: a `$(MAKE)` recipe is composed rather than launched, a depfile recipe is ordinary text, and a grouped double-colon action already carries its own `new_input_names`. Whoever takes this should probe each rather than assume the `$?` case is the only one.\n\nOwns tests/make/feature-vpath-a-recipe-read-early-spells-the-found-name-once, recorded from the oracle with a divergence marker naming this node. No upstream row is known to turn on it: features/vpathplus, the one suite case that reaches this machinery, does not name `$?`."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-22T06:25:19.059385573Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-22T07:08:30.195920833Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Delivered. The filing had the mechanism right and the CARRIER wrong, and the probe it asked for is what settled that: the other three early-read shapes are not only reachable, they were all wrong, and none of them has a `DeferredFreshness` to hang anything off.\n\nTHE MATRIX, every cell run through reference/make-oracle/make-4.4.1/make and then through Ronin, before anything moved. `VPATH = build`, `build/out.o` on disk, `out.o` absent, `ord.h` found at `build/ord.h`, and `$?` in the recipe to force the early read:\n\n  found current, read early     GNU `$^` `$<` `$+` all build/out.o, `$|` build/ord.h, `$?` build/out.o\n                                Ronin out.o / out.o / out.o / ord.h / build/out.o\n  remade here, read early       GNU and Ronin agree on `$^` `$<` `$+` `$?` — and `$|` DIVERGES ANYWAY.\n                                The order-only name was found and current whichever way the target went,\n                                so the filing's four-variable list was one short: `$|` is wrong in BOTH cells.\n  the same two cells, read late both tools agree on all four. The late path was already right.\n  `$(^D) $(^F) $(<D) $(<F)`     GNU build / out.o / build / out.o; Ronin . / out.o / . / out.o —\n                                halving the written name rather than the found one.\n\nTHE OTHER THREE EARLY-READ SHAPES, which the filing said \"may not be reachable at all\" and asked whoever took this to probe rather than assume. All three are reachable and all three were wrong by exactly the same amount:\n  a recursive `$(MAKE)` line   `$^` out.o where GNU says build/out.o\n  a grouped `::` action        the same, once per record\n  a `.KATI_DEPFILE` recipe     the same\nThat is what decides the carrier. The filing proposed hanging the names off `DeferredFreshness`; three of the four shapes have no such structure, so the references ride BESIDE it — their own per-edge relation — and `resolve_deferred_new_inputs` fills both in one pass.\n\nWHAT THE MECHANISM IS. A reference per prerequisite and per form rather than one per list, which is the filing's own shape and turns out to be the better one: `$^` expands to `a.c ${KATI_SETTLED_0} b.c`, a word list with one word standing in, so anything that treats a word as a whole still works. Measured: `$(patsubst %,-I%,$^)` comes out right. What does NOT work is anything that reads INSIDE the word, and that is the boundary below.\n\n`DepNode::searched_inputs` is where a dependent learns its prerequisites' found paths — the filing named this gap exactly — recorded as each prerequisite is planned, from the map `resolve_vpaths` already fills, in `build_plan`'s two loops and in `build_double_action`'s two, which do not share them. `AutoCommandVar::settled_references` mints one reference per prerequisite this form is about to name, reusing an existing one where a recipe reads the same prerequisite twice, and `DepNode::settled_names` carries the pairs out through `SinkEdge::settled_names` to `Graph::settled_names`, where `Builder::resolve_settled_names` substitutes at launch — through the same `searched_at` + `found_name_stands` reading `$?` already used, so a recipe read early and one read late are answered the same way. The D and F halves are done a word at a time inside `eval_impl` wherever a reference is written, because `eval`'s own halving would read a reference as one word with no directory in it; where no reference is written the value is left whole and halved exactly where it always was.\n\nTWO GATES ON THE EMISSION, and both are the point rather than caution:\n* `new_inputs_timing == SchedulerBoundary`, which is the destination saying it binds late values. A manifest cannot, so nothing shaped like this ever reaches one — the equivalence gate runs the whole 297-makefile corpus through a destination that answers `RecipeShell` and finds 0 disagreements, which is the evidence.\n* `function_depth == 0`. A reference is a word whose content no function can read. WITHOUT this gate `$(filter %.o,$^)` matches nothing and `$(basename $^)` cuts nothing off — and, measured, that is a REGRESSION in the remade cell, where the two tools agreed before. So a value a function is about to read carries the name as written and answers as it always did. `Evaluator::function_depth` counts the two places kati dispatches a builtin.\n\nTHE BOUNDARY, recorded from both sides rather than described. `feature-vpath-a-function-reads-a-name-read-early-as-written` carries a divergence marker: with the name found and current, GNU Make's `$(filter %.o,$^)` is `build/out.o` and `$(basename $^)` is `build/out plain`, and Ronin says `out.o` and `out.o plain`. `feature-vpath-a-function-reads-a-remade-name-as-written` is the same makefile with the target remade here and NO marker: both tools agree, and that fixture is what the gate is holding.\n\nTEETH, each parked and the whole 1005-case build-intent corpus run against it:\n| parked | cases that fail |\n| no reference is ever written | 7 |\n| the reference is written inside a function argument too | 1 |\n| a `::` action does not record its searched prerequisites | 1 |\n| the halving is left to the whole value rather than done a word at a time | 1 |\n\nNINE FIXTURES, all recorded from the oracle: -a-recursive-recipe-spells-the-found-name, -a-double-colon-action-spells-the-found-name, -a-depfile-recipe-spells-the-found-name, -a-recipe-read-early-halves-the-found-name, -a-recipe-read-early-halves-a-mixed-list, -a-recipe-read-early-spells-an-order-only-name, -a-recipe-read-early-keeps-a-remade-name, -a-function-reads-a-remade-name-as-written, and -a-function-reads-a-name-read-early-as-written, which carries the marker. No existing recording was rewritten.\n\nMARKER RESOLVED: tests/make/feature-vpath-a-recipe-read-early-spells-the-found-name-once/divergence, deleted, now matching the oracle. Seven markers remain — one out, one in.\n\nNO UNIT TEST, and recorded rather than glossed. The substitution is a fact about a graph, a sink and a launcher together, and the nine oracle-recorded fixtures plus the four parked measurements are what hold it; the one property no fixture states — that a manifest destination never receives a reference — is held by the equivalence gate, which runs the corpus through exactly such a destination.\n\nkati on nplan/make-vpath-name-reaches-a-recipe-read-early at 8cfe38ea01a2f4303c9700b813fde97b05db7fd1, pushed before this pin. One Ronin function was extracted on the way — `declare_edge` crossed the density gate, so where the directory search left its two answers is now `record_searched_spellings` and the archive-member test is `names_an_archive_member`.\n\nGATES: fmt clean both trees; `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` clean; `scripts/check-lints.sh` clean; workspace tests 1004 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored, unmoved; make_port 4/4 over 1005 cases with no existing recording rewritten, seven divergence sidecars; conformance 336 normalised identical / 51 differing, 286 raw, unmoved; equivalence 297 makefiles / 280 graphs / 75 refused / 0 disagreements, unmoved; upstream inventory 1285 rows at 107 unclassified / 0 compiler / 24 interface / 1154 narration, no drift, COMPILER STAYS ZERO; `scripts/check-make-projects.sh all` built vim 9.2 in 15 s and zsh 5.9.2 with 36 modules in 27 s, both unmoved; ninja conformance 425/425 plus 10 differentials, 86 build-outcome cases, 3 invocation-boundary cases, persistence round trip and log content; `cargo test --workspace --no-default-features` 773 passed / 0 failed; `scripts/check-release.sh` green end to end. The recorded trap held: the Make-less binary at the shared debug path was rebuilt with `--features make` before anything after it was probed."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-22T07:08:40.400870179Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-22T07:35:02.699816843Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @errata
                        text "Two details of the note above were written before the commit gate had finished with the change, and the gate moved them.\n\nWHAT THE EXTRACTION ACTUALLY WAS. The note says one function was extracted and names `record_searched_spellings` and `names_an_archive_member`. The first is right; the second was tried, then given back. `src/make/sink.rs` was at the density cap of 50 functions before this change, so the file had to lose one for the change to add one: the two names the compiler invents for itself — `completion_proxy` and `recipe_stage_proxy`, the same loop twice over a different prefix and counter — are now `src/make/sink/invented.rs`, a child module, which is why they can still read the sink's own fields. `declare_edge` stayed under the line cap without `names_an_archive_member` because the block it now calls one function for used to be eight lines inline. On the same pass, `BuildGraph::set_searched_at` and `set_settled_names` became one `set_searched_spellings`: the sink says both halves of the search's answer at one point, so the boundary crossing is one call. No behaviour moved with any of it — the corpus was rerun after each step.\n\nTHE WORKSPACE TEST COUNT IS 1005, not the 1004 the note records. `src/make/sink/invented.rs` needed a test of its own to clear the test-footprint gate on a new module, and `make::sink::invented::tests::an_invented_name_is_never_reused` is it: each invented name is its own, and one the graph already holds is stepped over rather than handed out twice, which is why those are loops rather than a counter read once.\n\nEvery other gate number in the note stands, and all of them were measured again on the committed tree after these three edits: fmt clean; `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` clean; `scripts/check-lints.sh` clean; workspace tests 1005 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored; make_port 4/4 over 1005 cases; conformance 336 normalised identical / 51 differing, 286 raw; equivalence 297 / 280 / 75 / 0 disagreements; upstream inventory 1285 rows at 107 / 0 / 24 / 1154, no drift, compiler ZERO; vim 9.2 in 15 s and zsh 5.9.2 in 26 s; ninja conformance 425/425 plus every differential; `cargo test --workspace --no-default-features` 773 / 0; `scripts/check-release.sh` green end to end."
                        after_done true
