                    {
                        at 2026-08-24T00:15:25.771568931Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Errata to the boundary this node recorded: feature-vpath-a-function-reads-a-name-read-early-as-written, which carried this node's marker, now agrees with the oracle and its divergence sidecar is deleted (the make_port gate forced it — a recorded divergence that has been fixed fails). The fix is make-a-scheduler-bound-recipe-is-expanded-though-its-target-is-current: that fixture forced the early read by naming `$?`, and a `$?` recipe is no longer read early — it defers to launch like any other. Read late, `$^` carries the settled (vpath-relocated) name directly, so `$(filter %.o,$^)` and `$(basename $^)` read it whole and the function-depth==0 workaround this node installed is never consulted for a `$?` recipe.\n\nThe boundary itself stands for the three carriers still read early — a grouped `::` action, a `.KATI_DEPFILE` recipe, and a `$(MAKE)` line — where a searched-for name inside a function argument is still spelt as written. That boundary remains documented by this node's delivery note and is still gated from the other side by feature-vpath-a-function-reads-a-remade-name-as-written, which is unchanged."
