                    {
                        at 2026-08-22T13:32:36.898523881Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "The performance stage was measured after all, and it is green, so `scripts/check-release.sh` is complete on this tree.\n\n`scripts/check-performance.sh --warmups 2 --repetitions 15` run TWICE against the pinned Ninja, both exit 0, both while the host carried another tenant's build at a 15-minute load average of 21 to 22 — which is a harder test than a quiet host rather than an easier one, since a refusal is what load produces. The two workloads that have refused under load in this campaign both held: `clean-tree-noop` at 14.289 ms against Ninja's 21.729 and 13.545 against 21.728, a ratio of 0.66 and 0.62 against the recorded 0.65; `dependency-log-load` at 6.160 against 8.145 and 5.855 against 7.510, a ratio of 0.76 and 0.78 against the recorded 0.73 and inside the gate's 120% band. `large-manifest-parse` ran at 293 and 295 ms against Ninja's 602 and 591.\n\nWall clock on a loaded host is not a number to compare against a quiet-host baseline, and it is not offered as one. What it settles is the gate's verdict, which is a ratio between two binaries measured back to back in the same conditions."
