    {
        id ronin-dyndep-diagnostic-context
        title "Show the source context Ninja shows for a dyndep file"
        kind @fix
        sealed true
        log (
            {
                at 2026-08-09T20:00:25.622201031Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @note
                text "Measured on ronin-indent-error-location, 2026-08-09, against pinned Ninja b51a1e3. Not fixed there because that node's subject was where an indent is located, and the located line now agrees for every dyndep shape probed; what is left is the rendering.\n\nNinja reads a dyndep file with the same lexer and reports through the same `Lexer::Error`, so a dyndep diagnostic gets the quoted source line and the caret whenever its column is non-zero, and the terminating blank line when it is zero. Ronin's `DyndepError` (src/dyndep.rs:175) prints `{path}:{line}: {kind}` and stops — it never reaches `write_located` in src/error.rs, so *no* dyndep diagnostic has ever carried context.\n\n  dd file: `ninja_dyndep_version = 1\\nbuild out: dyndep\\n  # c`\n    ninja  rc=1  stderr: ninja: error: dd:3: expected variable name\n                         `  # c`\n                         `  ^ near here`\n    ronin  rc=1  stderr: ronin: error: dd:3: expected variable name\n\n  dd file: `  ninja_dyndep_version = 1\\n`\n    ninja  rc=1  stderr: ninja: error: dd:1: unexpected indent  + a blank line\n    ronin  rc=1  stderr: ronin: error: dd:1: unexpected indent  + no blank line\n\nThe span is already there and already correct: `DyndepError` holds a `SourceSpan`, and `scanner_error` carries the scanner's own span with its column. Only `error(scanner, line, kind)` forces `column = 0`, which is right for the checks it raises — those are Ninja's zero-column ones. So the change is to render through the located printer rather than to find the location. It is small; what it needs is a sweep of every dyndep diagnostic against real Ninja before and after, because it moves the bytes of all of them, and conformance BuildCases for the ones that gain a caret. 8 dyndep shapes are already probed in this node's scratch sweep; they are not the whole set.\n\nStatus agrees throughout (1), so this is a message-shape defect. No conformance case can be added for a dyndep diagnostic until it is fixed."
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-24T05:49:54.541176517Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-24T06:15:04.635686589Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Fixed, and the fix was larger than the filing framed it. Done on ronin main 37be5c9, ronin-only (no kati change). This is Ninja's own diagnostic voice, so matching upstream Ninja byte-for-byte IS the contract.\n\nWHAT THE FILING SAID vs WHAT IT WAS. The filing said the location was already correct and only the RENDERING was missing — route DyndepError through the located printer. Rendering was indeed missing, but the location was ALSO wrong for a whole class of errors, so the fix is two parts.\n\nPART 1 — rendering (as filed). Extracted write_source_context from write_located (src/error.rs): the source-line-and-caret / terminating-blank-line half, without the `error:` header. DyndepError's Display (src/dyndep.rs) now writes its `path:line: message` header and then calls it. The `error:` word is NOT added here — a dyndep error surfaces while a target is being added (add_target_node), so the target context that wraps it supplies `error:`, exactly as it does for every other error raised there. Confirmed by a marker probe: the wrapper prints `ronin: error: <DyndepError>`.\n\nPART 2 — location (NOT as filed). The filing said `error(scanner, line, kind)` forcing column 0 is \"right for the checks it raises — those are Ninja's zero-column ones.\" A sweep against pinned Ninja b51a1e3 refuted this: Ninja draws a caret for unsupported-version, order-only-inputs, validation, wrong-version-name, and more — all raised through that helper, which threw the column away. Rewrote error() to build its span from scanner.last_token() (Ninja's last_token_, carrying line AND column), the same source scanerror already uses; dropped the now-dead line parameter and the locals feeding it, and Scanner::line() with them. Two structural corrections fell out, each measured against Ninja:\n - parse_version now reads the whole `name = value` binding before judging the name, as Ninja's ParseLet does. So `notversion` alone is `expected '='` (was ExpectedVersion), and a wrong name carries the caret past the value, not under the name.\n - the top-level stray-`=` check marks the token with begin_token before erroring, as Ninja's PeekToken does, so it names its own line (dd:2) instead of the binding read before it (dd:1).\n\nPROBE TABLE — 31 dyndep diagnostic shapes through pinned Ninja b51a1e3 and Ronin, stdout+stderr+status compared byte for byte after normalising the product name. Before: every one carried no context; several also had the wrong column or line. After: all 31 match, rc 1 throughout. Shapes cover the two rendering halves (caret / blank line), every error() kind (unsupported version, order-only direct and after-implicit, validation, no-build-statement, explicit outputs/inputs, expected dyndep command, binding-not-restat, unexpected EOF, multiple statements, empty path, expected path), the version read-order variants (notversion=1, notversion, notversion=, empty value, no trailing newline), and the top-level paths (stray = before and after version, identifier without version, build before version, unexpected identifier).\n\nCONFORMANCE. Added 5 differential BuildCases to examples/conformance.rs, one per mechanism: the caret-rendering case, the blank-line (line-start) case, a semantic error that gained a caret (order-only inputs), the version read-order case (notversion=1), and the stray-= line-naming case. Each runs real Ninja and real Ronin and compares byte for byte. Build-outcome cases 87 -> 92 (86 before this batch; +1 was the regeneration-progress node).\n\nVERIFICATION (sandboxed, SANDBOX_MEM=16G): scripts/check-ninja-conformance.sh green — 425/425 upstream, 10 differential, 92 build-outcome each on its recorded status, 3 invocation, persistence + log content. cargo fmt --all --check clean; scripts/check-lints.sh clean (clippy -D warnings, ronin + kati); dyndep unit tests 86/0; the invalid_case unit tests are substring checks on the error KIND and are unaffected. Every existing unit test that fed a malformed version line still yields the same kind."
            }

            {
                at 2026-08-24T06:16:56.506076954Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @status
                text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
            }
        )
    }

